.TH fleetring-dev 1  FleetRing "FleetRing manual"
.SH NAME
fleetring\-dev \- Runs a node for development; `\-d` runs it in the background
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBfleetring dev\fR [\fB\-\-data\-dir\fR] [\fB\-\-port\fR] [\fB\-d\fR|\fB\-\-detach\fR] [\fB\-\-timeout\fR] [\fB\-\-log\-format\fR] [\fB\-q\fR|\fB\-\-quiet\fR] [\fB\-\-color\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] [\fIsubcommands\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Runs a node for development; `\-d` runs it in the background
.PP
One node, on loopback only, with a local authority and an admin principal that every command can act as (ADR\-0039). The first run creates them, with the node\*(Aqs configuration, in the directory; later runs reuse them. Every start writes the `dev` context and makes it current unless another context is, so the other commands need no flags. `dev stop`, `dev status` and `dev logs` act on the node `\-d` started. Not for production.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-data\-dir\fR \fI<DATA_DIR>\fR
The dev directory; `~/.fleetring` by default

It holds the authority, the certificates, the configuration, and the databases.
.TP
\fB\-\-port\fR \fI<PORT>\fR
The loopback port the node serves on; 7400 by default

The admin listener takes the next one. Only the first run chooses it: later runs read it from `<dir>/fleetringd.toml`, and refuse a different one.
.TP
\fB\-d\fR, \fB\-\-detach\fR
Runs the dev node in the background, and returns once it is ready

Its output goes to `<dir>/fleetring.log`.
.TP
\fB\-\-timeout\fR \fI<TIMEOUT>\fR
How long `\-d` waits for the node to be ready: `<n>m` or `<n>s`

60s by default.
.TP
\fB\-\-log\-format\fR \fI<LOG_FORMAT>\fR
Writes log lines as `text` or `json`

Overrides `FLEETRING_LOG_FORMAT` and the configuration file\*(Aqs `[log] format`.
.TP
\fB\-q\fR, \fB\-\-quiet\fR
Prints the result and errors only

No progress, notes, warnings or override warnings. A command with no result then prints nothing.
.TP
\fB\-\-color\fR \fI<COLOR>\fR [default: auto]
When to colour log lines and the picker

`auto` colours on a terminal unless `NO_COLOR` is set or `TERM` is `dumb`; `always` and `never` do as they say.
.br

.br
\fIPossible values:\fR
.RS 14
.IP \(bu 2
auto: On a terminal, unless `NO_COLOR` is set or `TERM` is `dumb`
.IP \(bu 2
always: Always, even into a pipe or a file
.IP \(bu 2
never: Never
.RE
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help (see a summary with \*(Aq\-h\*(Aq)
.SH SUBCOMMANDS
.TP
fleetring\-dev\-stop(1)
Stops the dev node: drains it, and waits until it has exited
.TP
fleetring\-dev\-status(1)
Says whether the dev node runs, with its PID, address and release
.TP
fleetring\-dev\-logs(1)
Prints the log `dev \-d` writes
